WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
- "Study Finds 87% of
Chinese Takeout Eaten

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.170
by Team of Prosecutors Embroiled

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.087
in Late-Night Investigations."

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.340
I love that trope.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.260
It's so funny that, you know,

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.470
whether it is prosecutors
or corporate lawyers,

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:18.150
they're all in front of a big
table, late into the night,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.140
and then they just get box
after box of Chinese takeout.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.700
And they have some brilliant idea

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.160
while shoving lo mein into their mouth.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.170
The Onion is by far the best source

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.120
of satirical news on the internet.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.200
And they have, on occasion,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.330
taken shots at the legal profession.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.430
But the best satire has a grain of truth.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.653
So let's see how The Onion does

00:00:37.653 --> 00:00:39.903
when they make legal headlines.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.297
All right. So right off the bat.

00:00:43.297 --> 00:00:46.197
"Jurisprudence Fetishist
Gets Off on a Technicality."

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.170
That's sick (beep).

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.563
Probably something twisted like SMJ.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.890
Oh my God, I can't believe I just made

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.010
a subject matter jurisdiction/BDSM joke.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.950
That is that, that is a heck
of a way to start this video.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:02.783
Amazing.

00:01:04.687 --> 00:01:07.230
"Ketanji Brown Jackson Weighs History

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.810
Against Soul-Crushing
Thought of Spending Time

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:10.643
with These People."

00:01:10.643 --> 00:01:12.060
Ooh.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.460
Okay, I really think that the thought

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.420
that the members of the
Supreme Court are not friends

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.850
with each other or at least
professional with each other,

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.260
I think that's completely overblown.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.270
I think despite their
political differences,

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.480
I think probably most of the
people on the Supreme Court

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.860
are perfectly fine with each other

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:29.940
and the people on the Supreme Court

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.370
are perfectly fine human beings.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.760
I don't think Ketanji Brown Jackson

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.100
will have much of a decision to make here.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.543
She's gonna make history.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.500
All right, "Class-Action Suit Against God

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.037
Pays Out 45 Extra Seconds
of Life to Every Creature."

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.140
Ooh, that hits close to the home.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.090
Especially given the number
of class-action suits

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.207
I've covered.

00:01:52.207 --> 00:01:54.810
"Calling it a historic victory
for all who have been victims

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.250
of the Lord's negligence,

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.750
lawyers represented the planet's estimated

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.540
20 quintillion animal
inhabitants announced Tuesday

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.070
that a class-action lawsuit against God

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.590
would pay out an extra 45
seconds of life to each creature.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.660
Lead attorney Landon Burke
announced that anyone

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.030
who believed they were
owed restitution by God

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.890
could reply to the notice
they received in the mail

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.570
or sign up online to
receive their supplemental

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.190
45 seconds of life."

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.030
That's really funny

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.570
because that is often how
you have to provide the class

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.090
the restitution that they
get is through a postcard.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.400
It's a whole thing in federal court

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.320
or going to this really janky website

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.850
that always looks like a scam.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:31.850
Why do the class-action
websites always look terrible?

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:32.963
People don't sign up

00:02:32.963 --> 00:02:34.560
because they think that
they're being scammed

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.630
when often it's legit.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.460
I mean, class-action
lawsuits are notorious

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.410
for paying out really
small amounts of money

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.020
or coupons to the class.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.700
Often the only people who get rich

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.620
are the class-action lawyers.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.570
So actually in this
case, this is brilliant.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.330
If you actually were
a plaintiff's attorney

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:56.040
and you got 45 seconds of life
for 20 quintillion animals,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.620
then effectively, you're 30 or 40%

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.620
of that quintillion animals'
seconds times 45 seconds.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.580
They'd live forever.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.080
It's always the plaintiff's attorneys

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.360
who get tons and tons of money,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.970
even if the class gets almost nothing.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.320
Plaintiff's attorneys, man.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:18.750
"Supreme Court Rules Gay Rights
Do Not Extend to Dessert."

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.167
That's, I mean, that's too
close to what actually happened.

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.350
"While homosexuals do have
the right to get married,

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.330
the right to equal treatment
does not cover instances

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.130
of pastry, cake, or candy."

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:33.600
All right, so the Supreme
Court case in question

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.370
is a little more nuanced than that,

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:37.770
but I get where they're
coming from on this one.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:41.220
All right, "Man Who Never
Missed 'Ally McBeal'

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.857
Back in the Day Joins
the Trump Legal Team."

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:48.990
Oh boy, it seems like, it
seems like only yesterday

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.420
that we were dealing with Donald Trump

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:55.050
and his team of horrible,
horrible lawyers.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.900
Honestly, if you were
comparing Rudy Giuliani

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.170
and Sydney Powell to someone
who never missed an episode

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.440
of "Ally McBeal," I think
that would be a fair fight.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.000
That would probably be fine.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.770
And the funniest thing about this article

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.270
is that it's from 2018.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:12.270
The worst Trump lawyers
hadn't even been retained

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.770
at that point.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.603
Man, we were so innocent back then.

00:04:17.527 --> 00:04:18.870
"Christ Sues Catholic Church

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.427
for Unlicensed Use of His Image."

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.460
"I never signed off on, nor do I endorse,

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.230
the sentiments behind
any of these candles,

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.750
plates, statues, paintings, none of it.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.310
I don't want to have my brand devalued

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.010
by a bunch of people just
trying to turn a quick buck

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:34.350
by slapping on a reproduction
of my wounded body

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.670
on a cross."

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.320
Ooh boy.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.410
